  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Stoqaxoqtl (whose 
alliances are too incompatible) and Medard (#17), degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  Thus endeth the adventures of Stoqaxoqtl for this year.

  Josh the gentle (#3) Treated with Stoqaxoqtl, but Stoqaxoqtl did not react 
favorably to his amicable noises.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings 
will see the wisdom of Treating.

  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Palomides (#130) has arrived in Veracruz from Arkansas Territory, 
attracted by the fine (or infamous?  ?)   reputation of its king.


  Here is the financial report for Stoqaxoqtl's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Stoqaxoqtl was left 
with 10 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tattoo, Squire to Ilmarinen
To: Stoqaxoqtl

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season Ilmarinen prepared to quench his 
thirst for glory.  He prepared his armies to defend Texas and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Tattoo, Squire to Ilmarinen


